WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.150
Antarctica: a continent buried under ice.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.150
Yet its rocks hold coal,
made from tropical plants.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.270
In 1912, a German
meteorologist, Alfred Wegener,

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.830
argued that the continents had drifted.

5
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.570
South America and Africa fit together.

6
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.690
The same fossil species
lie on both coasts,

7
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.690
now an ocean apart.

8
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.210
Yet scientists rejected the idea.

9
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.690
What force could move a continent?

10
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.710
Wegener died in 1930,
and the debate stalled.

11
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.590
So what finally proved that
continents really do move?

12
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.510
In this mission, you'll
look inside the Earth,

13
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.830
from the thin crust to
the iron and nickel core.

14
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.730
Then you'll rejoin the
southern continents,

15
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.570
and weigh which evidence
finally settled the argument.

16
00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.960
Your mission: find out what finally
proved that the continents move.
